version: "1.0.0"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   <- filled in after Zenodo mints it (docs/RELEASE.md)
repository-code: "https://github.com/Major-Project-Amrita/Cooperative-payload-transport-by-a-four-robot-formation"
keywords:
  - multi-robot systems
  - cooperative transport
  - local planning
  - benchmark
  - replication
  - MuJoCo
  - ROS 2
abstract: >-
  An open, replicated benchmark of twelve local steering laws (APF, VFH, FGM,
  DWA, lattice MPC, MPPI, four histogram variants, a learned DAgger policy and
  the proposed hybrid PA-VFH, which feeds a VFH+ decision layer with a learned
  predictive-occupancy network) for a team of 3 to 9 differential-drive robots
  carrying one rigid payload through eight warehouse layouts with moving
  traffic. Two independent implementations (MATLAB and Python/ROS 2) agree
  step for step at zero noise; the evaluation randomises the traffic phase per
  run, tunes every planner under an equal budget, separates ground-truth
  collision screening from deployable sensor-based and conformal learned
  safety monitors, and replicates selected cases in MuJoCo physics with a
  robot-parameter sweep. Simulation only.
